   "id": "bava_kamma.48b.11",
   "daf": "48b",
   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "וְאִם הִכְנִיס בִּרְשׁוּת – בַּעַל חָצֵר חַיָּיב [כּוּ׳]. אִיתְּמַר, רַב אָמַר: הִלְכְתָא כְּתַנָּא קַמָּא, וּשְׁמוּאֵל אָמַר: הִלְכְתָא כְּרַבִּי.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «But if he brought» the ox into the courtyard «with permission, the owner of the courtyard is liable» for the damage caused. Rabbi Yehuda HaNasi says: The homeowner is not liable in any of the cases in the mishna, even if he gave his permission for the items to be brought onto his premises, unless he explicitly accepts responsibility upon himself to safeguard them. It «was stated» that the Sages disagreed with regard to the halakha in this dispute: «Rav said» that «the halakha» is «in accordance with» the opinion of «the first tanna, and Shmuel said» that «the halakha» is «in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi» Yehuda HaNasi."
  }
 ],
